# doc-sensitive-paths — the shipping gate's Step 1.5 list, tailored to this repo.
#
# Read by the vendored `doc-check.sh` (gregoryfoster/skills#252). One path per
# line; blank lines and `#` comments ignored. This file REPLACES the built-in
# defaults rather than extending them, so anything the gate should flag has to
# appear below.
#
# Entries match whole path SEGMENTS at any depth, not just the start of the
# path: `pyproject.toml` covers the root file AND every `packages/*/pyproject.
# toml`, which on this uv workspace is the difference between the gate seeing a
# package rename and reporting a clean green (#297). Six of the twelve defaults
# — CHANGELOG.md, schema.sql, src/api/, src/models/, src/core/, .env.example —
# name nothing that exists here and are deliberately absent; upstream prints a
# note about any entry that matches no tracked file, and
# scripts/tests/test_doc_sensitive_paths.py fails on one.
#
# The list is narrower than a bare `src/` on purpose. `src/` would match every
# source file in the workspace, so every branch would exit 1 and the exit code
# would stop meaning anything. Each entry below names a surface some doc
# ENUMERATES, so a change to it plausibly dates that doc.

# The policy file and the orientation README — root and every workspace member's
# (AGENTS.md § Project Layout, docs/MODULES-*.md).
AGENTS.md
README.md

# Workspace membership, layer contracts, coverage profiles, dependency pins.
# AGENTS.md's six-layer table and import-linter contracts live in the root file;
# per-package ones carry the names docs/MODULES-*.md index.
pyproject.toml
uv.lock

# Schema shape and migration order — docs/COMMANDS.md § migrations, the DB role
# split in docs/DEPLOYMENT.md.
alembic/

# systemd units and the operational CLIs the docs index by name:
# docs/DEPLOYMENT.md's service table, docs/COMMANDS*.md.
deploy/
scripts/

# The agent-context surface itself. docs/SKILLS.md describes the symlink layout
# and the .skills knobs; docs/SOCRATICODE.md describes the manifest and the
# session hooks; AGENTS.md § Agent Skills points at both.
.claude/
.skills/
.socraticodecontextartifacts.json
.pre-commit-config.yaml
.github/

# Enumerated code surfaces. The read-only route table is docs/API.md; the CLI
# entry points are docs/COMMANDS.md. `descriptors/` was the third — the PM
# producer descriptors, documented in docs/MODULES-SYNC-PRODUCERS.md and
# docs/LWW-NOOP-GATE.md — and #314 deleted the tree it pointed at. Dropped
# rather than kept as a dead entry: `test_every_entry_matches_a_tracked_file`
# refuses a list that cannot hit anything, which is what keeps the gate from
# printing the same green for "no sensitive paths touched" and "the list rotted".
api/v1/
cli/
